• I remember everything in our current chat, but I don’t automatically recall
  every past session word-for-word.

  You can reopen an earlier Codex conversation:

  - In the Codex app: search/select it from your chat history (Ctrl/Cmd + G).
  - In the Codex CLI: run codex resume, or codex resume --last.
  - To branch an old conversation without changing it: use codex fork.

  Codex may also retain selected preferences or summaries through Memory, but
  that’s separate from reopening the complete chat. You can manage it with /
  memories; ChatGPT’s memory is managed under Settings → Personalization.

  So yes—the closest equivalent to normal ChatGPT is to open/resume the old
  chat. Once resumed, I’ll have that conversation’s context again.


